{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["people_table:read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"description":"List a job\u2019s People table changes, oldest first (people_table.changes.list): custom cells (by jobPersonId), columns, views, your own preferences, the job default and Agent-notes metadata (never a note body or preview). Only settled changes are listed (settledThrough); a slower write arrives on a later call. Pass since on the first call; every call returns page.nextCursor, which you keep and pass back as cursor to read what changed next. A PERSON value naming a person you cannot see reads null; changes about such a person, and another member\u2019s PERSONAL views and preferences, are not listed. Built-in columns have no events: query rows again. A cursor older than 30 days is CHANGES_CURSOR_EXPIRED. Columns are addressed by id (country, custom:<fieldId>). Contact, financial and compliance columns are redacted for API keys and read exactly like unknown columns (COLUMN_NOT_QUERYABLE); Project To-do columns also need project_todos:read and Screening lms:read; candidate-written text (profile title, city, skills and other tag lists) is scrubbed of contact data and the surname and is selectable only. Names are the public \"First L.\" (else \"Unnamed candidate\") and selectable only: no search, filter, sort or facet runs on a name, and a query with no sort returns a stable order that is not by name. Address a person by jobPersonId. Banned, closed and non-visible candidates never appear in rows, counts or facets. Reads spend the key\u2019s budget (120 requests a minute and 50,000 rows an hour across jobs and surfaces); a spent budget is a 429 RATE_LIMITED with a retry delay. Requires people_table:read.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"page.nextCursor from the previous call; keep the last one to poll from.","maxLength":1024,"minLength":1